        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://coalcampusa.com/westpa/pittsburgh/muse/muse.htm",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Frick & Company founded Muse as a company coal town in the early 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Muse%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Muse ranks among the last coal towns constructed in the Pittsburgh area, dating back to 1923.",
